        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Hpmc (225 mg, 1.2 mmol) and hydrated neodymium chloride (213 mg, 0.6 mmol) were dissolved in methanol in a round-bottomed flask. Excess triethylamine (1 mL) was added slowly dropwise and the reaction was stirred for 12 h. The solvent was removed and the residue was stirred in toluene (~2 mL) for 1 h, then filtered to remove salts and left in an open vial to evaporate slowly, giving pale yellow crystals harvested before complete solvent loss.",
